# Per-instance script hooks. Each is optional; a plain install has none.
#
# watchdog-checks.sh — the instance's own watchdog checks (scripts/watchdog.sh).
#   Sourced near the top of watchdog.sh, so it only defines functions:
#     _ext_incident_label <key>  echo a label for one of its incident keys and
#                                return 0; return 1 for any other key
#     _ext_watchdog_checks       run once per tick, after the weekly-review
#                                check; everything watchdog.sh defines
#                                (incident_*, notify, log, ISSUES) is in scope
#
# context-sync-tick.sh — the instance's own work that rides the context-sync
#   tick (scripts/trigger-context-sync.sh): executed before the sync, capped at
#   2 min, output discarded, never fatal.
#
# Modules here belong to this installation, not to the kernel.
